      <!-- SECTION 3 -->
      <h2 id="execution-lifecycle">03 · EXECUTION LIFECYCLE AND OMM ENGINE</h2>
      <p>What happens on Salesforce servers when an email send with AMPscript is triggered?</p>

      <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1.5rem; margin:1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; color:var(--neon-pink); margin-bottom:1rem;">🔄 AN EMAIL'S JOURNEY: FROM CODE TO INBOX</div>
        
        <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0.9rem; font-size:0.88rem;">
          <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.8rem;">
            <span style="background:var(--neon-cyan); color:#000; font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; padding:0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius:3px; flex-shrink:0;">STEP 1</span>
            <div><strong>Subscriber Context Initialization:</strong> The send engine loads a row from the target Data Extension or send list for the current subscriber.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.8rem;">
            <span style="background:var(--neon-pink); color:#fff; font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; padding:0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius:3px; flex-shrink:0;">STEP 2</span>
            <div><strong>OMM (Output Messaging Machine) Execution:</strong> The parser reads the email body <em>top-to-bottom</em>. It executes <code>%%[ ... ]%%</code> blocks, evaluates logic, and runs data queries.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.8rem;">
            <span style="background:var(--neon-yellow); color:#000; font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; padding:0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius:3px; flex-shrink:0;">STEP 3</span>
            <div><strong>Inline Injection:</strong> Output tags like <code>%%=v(@Name)=%%</code> are replaced with final HTML or text strings.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.8rem;">
            <span style="background:var(--neon-green); color:#000; font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; padding:0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius:3px; flex-shrink:0;">STEP 4</span>
            <div><strong>MTA Dispatch:</strong> The final rendered email (clean of any Marketing Cloud code) is dispatched to the recipient's mail server.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        <div class="callout-label">💡 PRO TIP · CASE INSENSITIVITY</div>
        AMPscript is <strong>case-insensitive</strong>. <code>SET @name = "John"</code>, <code>set @Name = "John"</code> and <code>Set @NAME = "John"</code> are identical to the engine. However, adhering to standard conventions like <em>camelCase</em> ensures clean, maintainable code.
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 4 -->
      <h2 id="basic-syntax">04 · BASIC SYNTAX AND DELIMITER TYPES</h2>
      <p>There are two primary ways to write AMPscript depending on your objective:</p>

      <h3>1. Multiline Code Blocks: <code>%%[ ... ]%%</code></h3>
      <p>Used for variable declarations, math operations, function calls, and conditional logic. Everything inside executes silently without rendering visible text.</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="code-lang">AMPSCRIPT · DECLARATION & ASSIGNMENT</span>
          <button class="btn-copy" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.closest('.code-block').querySelector('pre').innerText); this.textContent='COPIED!'; setTimeout(()=>this.textContent='COPY',2000);">COPY</button>
        </div>
        <pre><code class="language-ampscript">%%[
  /* 1. Declare variables using the VAR keyword */
  VAR @name, @tier, @points, @discount

  /* 2. Assign values using SET */
  SET @name = "Holwan David"
  SET @tier = "VIP"
  SET @points = 1250

  /* 3. Conditional logic */
  IF @tier == "VIP" THEN
    SET @discount = 20
  ELSE
    SET @discount = 5
  ENDIF
]%%</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h3>2. Inline Output Delimiters: <code>%%= ... =%%</code></h3>
      <p>Used directly inside HTML tags or text paragraphs to <strong>output the value of a variable or function result</strong>:</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="code-lang">HTML + INLINE AMPSCRIPT</span>
          <button class="btn-copy" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.closest('.code-block').querySelector('pre').innerText); this.textContent='COPIED!'; setTimeout(()=>this.textContent='COPY',2000);">COPY</button>
        </div>
        <pre><code class="language-html">&lt;!-- Inline variable output in HTML --&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Hello, %%=v(@name)=%%!&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your member tier is &lt;strong&gt;%%=v(@tier)=%%&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have a &lt;span style="color:#00ffff;"&gt;%%=v(@discount)=%% % discount&lt;/span&gt; available.&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 5 -->
      <h2 id="control-flow">05 · CONTROL FLOW: IF / ELSE CONDITIONAL STATEMENTS</h2>
      <p>Conditional logic enables dynamic content rendering tailored to each subscriber's unique profile:</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-header">
          <span class="code-lang">AMPSCRIPT · IF / ELSEIF / ELSE STRUCTURE</span>
          <button class="btn-copy" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(this.closest('.code-block').querySelector('pre').innerText); this.textContent='COPIED!'; setTimeout(()=>this.textContent='COPY',2000);">COPY</button>
        </div>
        <pre><code class="language-ampscript">%%[
  VAR @tier, @message

  SET @tier = AttributeValue("CustomerTier")

  IF @tier == "Platinum" THEN
    SET @message = "Exclusive VIP lounge access and unlimited free shipping."
  ELSEIF @tier == "Gold" THEN
    SET @message = "Enjoy a 15% discount on your next purchase."
  ELSE
    SET @message = "Earn reward points on every order to level up."
  ENDIF
]%%

&lt;!-- In email template --&gt;
&lt;div class="promo-box"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;%%=v(@message)=%%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 6 -->
      <h2 id="essential-functions">06 · ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS FOR YOUR FIRST PROJECT</h2>
      <p>Key fundamental functions every SFMC developer must know:</p>

      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        
        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-cyan); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">AttributeValue("Field")</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Safely retrieves a subscriber attribute. If the field is missing or null, it returns an empty string instead of crashing the send.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-pink); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">Empty(@var)</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Returns <code>True</code> if the variable is null, empty string, or undefined. Essential for defensive programming.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-yellow); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">v(@var)</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Outputs variable content safely in inline mode.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-green); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">Concat("Text1", @var, "Text2")</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Concatenates multiple strings and variables into a single result.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-purple); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">ProperCase(@name)</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Capitalizes the first letter of each word. Perfect for cleaning messy raw database names.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-cyan); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">FormatDate(Now(), "yyyy-MM-dd")</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Formats date and time values into standardized readable patterns.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 7 -->
      <h2 id="best-practices">07 · GOLDEN RULES FOR AMPSCRIPT DEVELOPMENT</h2>
      <ol style="padding-left:1.2rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:0.9rem;">
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Always declare variables with <code>VAR</code>:</strong> Declaring variables at the top of your block prevents scoping issues and improves maintainability.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Wrap send context fields with <code>AttributeValue()</code>:</strong> Calling <code>[FieldName]</code> directly causes a hard send failure if the column doesn't exist in the Send DE. <code>AttributeValue()</code> fails safely.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Centralize control logic in the email header:</strong> Keep a primary <code>%%[ ... ]%%</code> block at the very top of your email and keep the HTML body clean with <code>%%=v(@var)=%%</code>.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Always test edge cases in Preview & Test:</strong> Verify behavior when a subscriber's first name or attribute is blank.</li>
      </ol>

